cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use FrameIt, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
title: "FrameIt: Focused Regional Analysis of Modeled Events with Integrated Tracking"
abstract: >-
  FrameIt is a modular Python library for tracking atmospheric events in
  numerical model outputs and extracting a moving sub-domain centred on them.
  It reads and normalises outputs from several models, locates the event with
  one of four tracking methods, and writes the surrounding fields as
  self-contained NetCDF files on the model native cartesian grid and on a
  geodesic polar grid. It is designed to reduce the volume of regional,
  kilometre-scale simulations to datasets that can be archived and shared.
type: software
